3890  GestureDetector         com.nobody.myapp                     I  handleMessage TAP\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2703370376/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2703398073","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103572#issuecomment-2703398073","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103572","id":2703398073,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hIpS5","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T10:12:27Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T10:12:27Z","body":"> 2025-03-06 15:30:04.928  3890-4136  godot                   com.nobody.myapp                     E  SCRIPT ERROR: Invalid call to function 'vibrate' in base 'JavaObject'. Expected 5 arguments.\n> 2025-03-06 15:30:04.928  3890-4136  godot                   com.nobody.myapp                     E     at: _on_button_pressed (res://node_2d.gd:25)\n\nThe \"5 arguments\" seems a bit weird, but based on the API reference, it seems like `vibrate` takes two arguments (at least the latest non-deprecated version... not sure how our interface deals with the polymorphism there).\n\nhttps://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Vibrator#vibrate(android.os.VibrationEffect,%20android.os.VibrationAttributes)\n\nMaybe Godot reports 5 because 3 are taken by the Godot <> Java mapping? If so we might need to tweak that to report a clearer count that matches the Java API.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2703398073/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2703465212","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103572#issuecomment-2703465212","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103572","id":2703465212,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hI5r8","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T10:39:44Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T10:40:54Z","body":"> SCRIPT ERROR: Invalid call to function 'vibrate' in base 'JavaObject'. Expected 5 arguments.\n\nHmm... Not sure where the mention of \"5 arguments\" came from. I tested it again on my device (Moto G9 with Android 11 and Xiaomi with Android 14) and couldn't reproduce the issue. It works as expected.\n\n> based on the API reference, it seems like vibrate takes two arguments\n\nThe vibrate method is overloaded -- it also accepts a single argument, which is the expected usage here: https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Vibrator#vibrate(android.os.VibrationEffect)\n\nCC @dsnopek @m4gr3d ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2703465212/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704738051","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103572#issuecomment-2704738051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103572","id":2704738051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hNwcD","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T19:19:25Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T19:19:25Z","body":"@syntaxerror247 Are you testing on `master` or Godot 4.4-stable? This may be related to the issues @dsnopek fixed, which means the code would only work on `master` and not in `4.4-stable`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704738051/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704748457","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103572#issuecomment-2704748457","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103572","id":2704748457,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hNy-p","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T19:24:38Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T19:24:38Z","body":"> Maybe Godot reports 5 because 3 are taken by the Godot <> Java mapping? If so we might need to tweak that to report a clearer count that matches the Java API.\n\nNo, that shouldn't be the case. The only way a 2 argument method could get the \"Expected 5 arguments\" message would be due to a bug.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704748457/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704763481","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103572#issuecomment-2704763481","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103572","id":2704763481,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hN2pZ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T19:31:50Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T19:32:27Z","body":"I just tested myself with Godot 4.4-stable, using a slightly cut down version of the code given above:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc test_vibration():\n\tvar android_runtime = Engine.get_singleton(\"AndroidRuntime\")\n\tif android_runtime:\n\t\tprint(\"Checking if the device supports vibration\")\n\t\tvar vibrator_service = android_runtime.getApplicationContext().getSystemService(\"vibrator\")\n\t\tif vibrator_service:\n\t\t\tif vibrator_service.hasVibrator():\n\t\t\t\tprint(\"Vibration is supported on device! Vibrating now...\")\n\t\t\t\tvar VibrationEffect = JavaClassWrapper.wrap(\"android.os.VibrationEffect\")\n\t\t\t\tvar effect = VibrationEffect.createOneShot(500, VibrationEffect.DEFAULT_AMPLITUDE)\n\t\t\t\tvibrator_service.vibrate(effect)\n\t\t\telse:\n\t\t\t\tprinterr(\"Vibration is not supported on device\")\n\t\telse:\n\t\t\tprinterr(\"Unable to retrieve the vibrator service\")\n\telse:\n\t\tprinterr(\"Couldn't find AndroidRuntime singleton\")\n```\n\nAnd it worked for me! No error about \"Expected 5 arguments\", and I did get the vibration, but it's worth pointing out that you need to enable the \"Vibrate\" permission in the export settings for your Android preset:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0ad9a56c-611d-47fe-be6c-10d0e904c85d)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704763481/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2705191692","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103572#issuecomment-2705191692","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103572","id":2705191692,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hPfMM","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T23:49:45Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T23:49:45Z","body":"> @syntaxerror247 Are you testing on `master` or Godot 4.4-stable? This may be related to the issues @dsnopek fixed, which means the code would only work on `master` and not in `4.4-stable`.\n\nI tested with both 4.4-stable and master.\n\nThe only conclusion I can think of now is that this might be a device-specific issue. @BraveEvidence, could you please share your testing device details?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2705191692/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2705307095","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103572#issuecomment-2705307095","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103572"